"text":"வந்து","lemma":"vantu","gloss":"having come"}],"gloss":"fearfully"},{"surface":"அன்று","parts":[{"text":"அன்று","lemma":"aṉṟu","gloss":"it is of that nature"}],"gloss":"it is"},{"surface":"இம்","parts":[{"text":"இம்","lemma":"இம்","gloss":"this"}],"gloss":"this","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மஞ்சுபடு","parts":[{"text":"மஞ்சு","lemma":"mañcu","gloss":"mist/clouds"},{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"resting/occurring"}],"gloss":"mist-covered"},{"surface":"முதுகாடு","parts":[{"text":"முது","lemma":"mutu","gloss":"ancient/old"},{"text":"காடு","lemma":"kāṭu","gloss":"forest/crematorium"}],"gloss":"ancient crematorium"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நெஞ்சமர்","parts":[{"text":"நெஞ்சு","lemma":"neñcu","gloss":"heart"},{"text":"அமர்","lemma":"amar","gloss":"abide/desire"}],"gloss":"beloved of the heart"},{"surface":"காதலர்","parts":[{"text":"காதல்","lemma":"kātal","gloss":"love"},{"text":"அர்","lemma":"-ar","gloss":"pronominal suffix (plural/honorific)"}],"gloss":"lovers"},{"surface":"அழுத","parts":[{"text":"அழு","lemma":"aḻu","gloss":"weep"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"-t-","gloss":"past tense infix"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"-a","gloss":"relative participle suffix"}],"gloss":"wept"},{"surface":"கண்ணீர்","parts":[{"text":"கண்","lemma":"kaṇ","gloss":"eye"},{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"nīr","gloss":"water"}],"gloss":"tears"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"என்புபடு","parts":[{"text":"என்பு","lemma":"eṉpu","gloss":"bone"},{"text":"படு","lemma":"paṭu","gloss":"lying/occurring"}],"gloss":"where bones lie"},{"surface":"சுடலை","parts":[{"text":"சுடலை","lemma":"cuṭalai","gloss":"crematorium"}],"gloss":"crematorium"},{"surface":"வெண்ணீறு","parts":[{"text":"வெள்","lemma":"veḷ","gloss":"white"},{"text":"நீறு","lemma":"nīṟu","gloss":"ashes"}],"gloss":"white ashes"},{"surface":"அவிப்ப","parts":[{"text":"அவி","lemma":"avi","gloss":"extinguish"},{"text":"ப்ப","lemma":"-ppa","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to extinguish"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"எல்லார்","parts":[{"text":"எல்லார்","lemma":"ellār","gloss":"everyone"}],"gloss":"everyone's"},{"surface":"புறனும்","parts":[{"text":"புறன்","lemma":"puṟaṉ","gloss":"back/end"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"-um","gloss":"even/also"}],"gloss":"even the back/end"},{"surface":"தான்","parts":[{"text":"தான்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"self"}],"gloss":"itself"},{"surface":"கண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கண்டு","lemma":"கண்டு","gloss":"having seen"}],"gloss":"having seen","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"உலகத்து","parts":[{"text":"உலகத்து","lemma":"உலகத்து","gloss":"of the world"}],"gloss":"of the world","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மன்பதைக்","parts":[{"text":"மன்பதைக்","lemma":"மன்பதைக்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கெல்லாம்","parts":[{"text":"கெல்லாம்","lemma":"கெல்லாம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தானாய்த்","parts":[{"text":"தானாய்த்","lemma":"தானாய்த்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true},{"words":[{"surface":"தன்புறம்","parts":[{"text":"தன்புறம்","lemma":"தன்புறம்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காண்போர்க்","parts":[{"text":"காண்போர்க்","lemma":"காண்போர்க்","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"காண்புஅறி","parts":[{"text":"காண்புஅறி","lemma":"காண்புஅறி","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"யாதே","parts":[{"text":"யாதே","lemma":"யாதே","gloss":""}],"gloss":"","split_unverified":true}],"as_printed":true}],"literal":"Saline wasteland having spread, spurge having grown high, / even in the daytime hooting, with the rock horned owl having crooked teeth, / by the light of the funeral pyre, with the ghoul women, / fearfully it is, this mist-covered ancient crematorium, / where the tears wept by the beloved of the heart / extinguish the white ashes of the crematorium where bones lie. / Having seen the end of everyone itself, of the world / to all living beings having become itself, / its own end, to those who see, is never known.","translation":"Spurge grows high on the sprawling saline wasteland. Even in the daytime, the rock-horned owl with crooked teeth hoots. In the light of the funeral pyres, ghoul-women wander. This mist-shrouded ancient crematorium is a terrifying place, where the tears wept by grieving lovers extinguish the white ashes of the pyres where bones lie. This place has seen the end of everyone in this world; it has become the ultimate destination for all living beings. Yet, its own end is never seen by anyone.","modern":"உவர் நிலம் பரவி, கள்ளிச் செடிகள் வளர்ந்து, பகலிலும் கோணல் பற்களை உடைய கூகை ஆந்தையுடன் சேர்ந்து அலறும், ஈம நெருப்பின் வெளிச்சத்தில் பேய் மகளிரோடு கூடி இருக்கும் இந்த மூடுபனி நிறைந்த சுடுகாடு அச்சம் தருவதாகும். நெஞ்சில் நிறைந்த காதலர்கள் அழுத கண்ணீர், எலும்புகள் கிடக்கும் சுடுகாட்டின் வெண்ணீற்றை அணைக்கிறது. உலகத்தில் உள்ள எல்லாரது முடிவையும் தான் கண்டு, உலகத்து உயிர்களுக்கெல்லாம் தானே முடிவாகி நிற்கும் இந்தச் சுடுகாடு, தன் முடிவைக் காண்பாரைக் கண்டதே இல்லை.","explanation":"The poet Tāyaṅkaṇṇaṉār describes the terrifying nature of the ancient crematorium (mutukāṭu) in this poem belonging to the Kāñci tiṇai (theme of impermanence). He paints a vivid picture of a desolate wasteland overgrown with spurge cacti, where owls hoot even during the day and ghoul-women dance by the light of funeral pyres. The emotional core of the poem lies in the image of grieving lovers whose tears are so abundant that they extinguish the hot white ashes of the pyres. The poet personifies the crematorium as an entity that has witnessed the end of every living being in the world, serving as the final destination for all. Yet, while it sees the end of everyone else, no one has ever lived to see the end of the crematorium itself, highlighting the absolute and eternal nature of death and impermanence.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}